.th RJESTAT "PWB I" 02/09/76
.sh NAME
rjestat \- RJE status and enquiries
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd rjestat
[
.bd \-
] [
.bd 158
] [
.bd 168
] [
.bd 1110
]
.sh DESCRIPTION
When invoked without the `\-' argument,
.it rjestat
reports the current status of the RJE links
to the specified host computers.
When invoked with the `\-' argument,
.it rjestat
sets up an interactive status terminal.
If no hosts are cited explicitly,
the specification defaults to all those
for which a given UNIX is configured.
.s3
To enter an enquiry via a status terminal,
you must first generate an interrupt.
This can be done by hitting the DEL key
or the BREAK/INTERRUPT button.
.it Rjestat
will respond by prompting for enquiries directed
to each host in turn.
The line on which a prompt appears may be completed
to form a legitimate display command for the particular host.
If the line is terminated with a `\\',
the prompt will be repeated,
otherwise it will advance to the next host.
A carriage return alone indicates
that no enquiry is to be directed to a particular host.
For example,
.s3
.in +6
\fI158: /*$d\fRi\\
.br
\fI158: /*$d\fRq,xeq
.br
\fI168: /*$d\fR
.br
\fI1110: @@d\fRa
.in -6
.s3
You should expect to wait at least 30 seconds for a response.
.s3
An interrupt will temporarily halt
the display of responses.
It can therefore be used to inhibit roll-up
on a CRT terminal.
The display of responses will resume
after all prompts have been satisfied
(perhaps by null completions).
.s3
To exit from the status terminal, generate a quit signal
or type DEL followed by EOT.
.sh FILES
/dev/rje*	  DQS11's used by RJE
.br
/usr/rje/sys	  UNIX system
.br
/usr/rje/lines	  configuration table
.s3
And, in the directory for each RJE subsystem,
.s3
log		  activity log
.br
resp		  concatenated responses
.br
status		  message of the day
.br
xmit*		  files queued
.br
*mesg		  enquiry slot
.br
*init		  boot program
